  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'third places' was first introduced by sociologist Ray Oldenburg in his book 'The Great Good Place'. According to Oldenburg, third places are public spaces where people gather to socialize and relax outside the confines of home (first place) and work (second place). These places can be coffee shops, parks, libraries, or even bars. They serve as a vital part of a community's social fabric by providing a neutral ground for people from different backgrounds to interact.\n\nIn today's fast-paced world, third places are more important than ever. With the rise of technology and social media, many people spend most of their time at home or in front of screens. As a result, face-to-face interactions have decreased significantly. Third places offer a much-needed respite from this isolation by providing opportunities for people to engage with others in a relaxed environment.\n\nHowever, not all third places are created equal. Some may be too loud or crowded, while others may be too expensive or exclusive. It's essential to find the right balance between comfort and accessibility when choosing a third place. By doing so, individuals can reap the benefits of socializing without sacrificing their personal space.\n\nIn conclusion, third places play a crucial role in fostering community connections and promoting social well-being. As we continue to navigate the complexities of modern life, it's essential to prioritize these public spaces and make them an integral part of our daily routines.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is a 'third place', according to Ray Oldenburg?\",\n      \"options\": [\"A private space where people can relax at home\", \"A public space where people gather outside work and home\", \"A social media platform for online interactions\", \"A type of restaurant serving only coffee\"],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What is a consequence of increased screen time, according to the text?\",\n      \"options\": [\"People become more isolated and lonely\", \"They start to enjoy reading more books\", \"Their social skills improve significantly\", \"They begin to spend less money on entertainment\"],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards third places?\",\n      \"options\": [\"He thinks they are unnecessary and a waste of time\", \"He believes they can be beneficial for socializing but only if chosen wisely\", \"He sees them as a threat to traditional community values\", \"He thinks they should be avoided due to their high costs\"],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the text?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The importance of social media in modern life\", \"The benefits of third places for community connections\", \"The drawbacks of technology on human relationships\", \"The need for more public spaces in urban areas\"],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"According to the text, what is a key factor when choosing a third place?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Its proximity to work or home\", \"Its affordability and accessibility for all\", \"The type of food it serves\", \"The level of noise and crowd it generates\"],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
